The complete picture:

1. **Guest-fatal destructor suppression** ([prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc)): `guest-fatal` now sets exit-status 255 and freeze-marks all finalizable objects destructed before the ordinary shutdown runs, so shutdown functions and buffers still flow but destructors stay silent ("BS", never "BSD"). `run-main` falls back to 255 for shutdown-phase guest fatals. All fatal fixtures pin `:status 255`, plus a new `:trigger-user-error-suppresses-destructors` fixture (live `__destruct` object + shutdown fn + echo → `BS`).

2. **Stream P2, fully** ([prelude.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc), [lower.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc), [portable_harness.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/test/yang/php/antlr/portable_harness.cljc)): lowering never embeds composition data — `:request-node`/`:response-node`/`:diag-node` are opaque operands spliced by the harness. `run-lifecycle-raw` attaches both stream handles to the walker VM (sealed refs via `engine/attach-resource`) and passes them as `run-main` operands; `emit-response!`/`warn-sink` `stream/put!` onto them **during execution**, the runtime no longer touches the cells on this path, and the post-completion `emit-all!` copy is deleted — with it gone and gates green, the records provably arrived via in-VM effects. `run-main` drains each stream (fresh oldest cursor + `poll!` loop) and folds through `response-view`, so header replacement is interpreted from appended commands. The `stream` module is registered in both portable registries; stream-less compositions (e2e, linked, prelude tests) pass two operands and use cells exactly as before. New `lowering-splices-stream-operands-test` pins the 4-operand splice and 2-operand default. One real bug caught by tests along the way: omitted operands bind host `nil`, not `:php/null` — all stream-cell checks now test the keyword.

3. **HTTP/cookie residuals**: `http_response_code(0)` is a getter even after output; excess setcookie args throw `ArgumentCountError` with the exact PHP 8.3.35 wordings (verified against php-src head.c and zend_API.c); unknown/numeric option messages match head.c verbatim (`option "bogus" is invalid`, `option array cannot have numeric keys`); array-option coercions restored per slot. New fixtures for each probe.

4. **Oracle runner** ([oracle.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-b2/src/dev/yang/php/oracle.clj)): plain fatals populate `:fatal` only (`:uncaught nil`); `print-fold` carries `:fatal` and `:status`.

Verification: gates green — request-context + p5b2-lifecycle (8 tests, 188 assertions, 0 failures), plus prelude/class-model/lower-portable (49 tests, 2214 assertions, 0 failures); kondo clean on all touched files; final gate re-run done on the amended tree. Not run: e2e (missing generated TypeScriptLexer in this checkout, pre-existing) and the docker/shiva oracle (no docker on this laptop); all new fixtures stay `:oracle :pending` for the seat's pass.
